ody of the water meter in the form of a plastic frame that holds glass of display on the body of the water meter. The water meter cannot be accessed without damaging seal.\"\n}\n\nrevision_history: [{\"revision\": \"3\"}]. Hmm — with only revision number. I'll include it. Actually, wait: could \"Revision 3\" instead belong to revision_history of this cert revision list? The certificate is at Revision 3. I'll include {\"revision\": \"3\"} without date/changes fields (omit missing).\n\ntest_reports: none in fragment.\n\nLet me now also double check the model_id strings — using \"sonico NANO DN32 Q3=6.3 Q3/Q1=160\" is a bit long; repeated 44×5=220 times in matrix rows plus 44 in models plus 264 in model_level values. That's a lot of repetition but JSON handles it. Could shorten to \"DN32/6.3/160\". Shorter is better for payload. Let me use a compact scheme: \"sonico NANO DN32 Q3=6.3 R160\"? \"R\" prefix ambiguous. Use \"DN32 Q3=6.3 x160\"? Hmm.\n\nI'll use \"sonico NANO DN32 Q3=6.3 Q3/Q1=160\" — explicit beats compact. Actually, let me compromise: model_id \"DN32-Q3_6.3-R160\" is cryptic. Keep explicit. Fine.\n\nNow write the final JSON carefully, making sure numbers are numbers.\n\nLet me write matrix rows per table:\n\nTable 1 (DN32, ratios 160–500):\n[\n {\"model\": \"sonico NANO DN32 Q3=6.3 Q3/Q1=160\", \"nominal_diameter\": 32, \"q1\": 0.039, \"q2\": 0.063, \"q3\": 6.3, \"q4\": 7.875, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 160},\n {\"model\": \"sonico NANO DN32 Q3=10 Q3/Q1=160\", \"nominal_diameter\": 32, \"q1\": 0.063, \"q2\": 0.1, \"q3\": 10, \"q4\": 12.5, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 160},\n {\"model\": \"sonico NANO DN32 Q3=6.3 Q3/Q1=200\", ..., \"q1\": 0.032, \"q2\": 0.05, \"q3\": 6.3, \"q4\": 7.875, ratio 200},\n {\"model\": \"sonico NANO DN32 Q3=10 Q3/Q1=200\", \"q1\": 0.05, \"q2\": 0.08, \"q3\": 10, \"q4\": 12.5, 200},\n {\"model\": \"sonico NANO DN32 Q3=6.3 Q3/Q1=250\", \"q1\": 0.025, \"q2\": 0.04, \"q3\": 6.3, \"q4\": 7.875, 250},\n {\"model\": \"sonico NANO DN32 Q3=10 Q3/Q1=250\", \"q1\